## How rules and hooks reach a session

- **CLAUDE.md**: ancestors load at launch; a subdirectory `CLAUDE.md` loads
  when the agent first reads a file in that subtree. Not re-injected after
  `/compact` until a file there is read again.
- **`.claude/settings.json`** is read from the session's project root ONLY.
  So an identical copy of `.claude/hooks/` sits here and in every separate
  repo, and each hook finds the owning unit itself.
- **`.claude/specwright.ini`** names the units, their commands, the gate steps
  and every location. Hooks read it; edit it, never the hooks.
- Hooks: lint findings on every edit come back to you — fix them before moving
  on. The turn cannot end while typecheck fails in a unit you touched.

