## Working with other sessions

- Stage by path, never `git add -A` in a shared checkout.
- The supervisor (a person) owns commits, merges, pushes and migrations.
- Stop every server and container YOUR session started; kill by the pid
  listening on the port, after checking it is your checkout's. Never an
  unscoped `pkill -f` or `taskkill /im`.

